# Installing campusbot

Use a release binary for deployment. The usual layout is:

- `/opt/campusbot/bin/campusbot` for the binary
- `/etc/campusbot/zuliprc` for the bot credentials
- `/etc/campusbot/workers` for optional worker credentials
- `/var/lib/campusbot` for the SQLite database

Create a system user without a home directory:

```sh
sudo useradd --system --user-group --no-create-home \
  --home-dir /nonexistent --shell /usr/sbin/nologin campusbot
```

Install the binary and credentials:

```sh
sudo install -d -o root -g root -m 0755 /opt/campusbot/bin
sudo install -m 0755 ./campusbot /opt/campusbot/bin/campusbot

sudo install -d -o root -g campusbot -m 0750 /etc/campusbot /etc/campusbot/workers
sudo install -o root -g campusbot -m 0640 ./zuliprc /etc/campusbot/zuliprc

sudo install -d -o campusbot -g campusbot -m 0750 /var/lib/campusbot
```

Create `/etc/systemd/system/campusbot.service`:

```ini
[Unit]
Description=Campusbot Zulip bot
Wants=network-online.target
After=network-online.target

[Service]
Type=simple
User=campusbot
Group=campusbot
WorkingDirectory=/var/lib/campusbot
ExecStart=/opt/campusbot/bin/campusbot --zuliprc /etc/campusbot/zuliprc --worker-rc-dir /etc/campusbot/workers --db /var/lib/campusbot/campusbot.sqlite3 --log-format json
Restart=on-failure
RestartSec=5s
NoNewPrivileges=true
PrivateTmp=true
ProtectSystem=strict
ProtectHome=true
ReadWritePaths=/var/lib/campusbot

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
```

Enable and start the service:

```sh
sudo systemctl daemon-reload
sudo systemctl enable campusbot.service
sudo systemctl start campusbot.service
sudo systemctl status campusbot.service
```
